// The RMSnorm engine: one engine id serving the forward and backward packs. Forward and
// backward have disjoint node-attribute topologies, so graph_match tries each in turn and
// binds only which one matched; both packs' dispatch handlers re-derive every operand
// from the graph node directly, exactly as the plans they wrap always have. The two
// packs share one KMD and one UHD (a single-kernel pack has nothing to rank either way),
// so splitting them into two engines would duplicate an identical heuristic and schema
// for no reason -- the Pointwise add/mul shape, not the Pointwise/PointwiseSub one.
//
// sdk_version floors the engine at the plugin API that carries runtime pass-by-value
// scalars: epsilon may arrive as a user-supplied value at execute rather than baked in,
// and an engine claiming only the baseline is filtered out of such a graph entirely.
